<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>
  <!--
    World module strings (src/World/). Covers the world map, settlements,
    caravan formation/split, route planning (waypoint editor for caravan
    travel), gear-equip menu (pawn-side equip/swap from Caravan Inspect),
    settlement and quest browsers, world scanner (mirrors Map.Scanner's
    category structure), caravan multi-select, layer switching, and the
    stat-breakdown overlay.

    Files contributing strings:
      - WorldNavigationState.cs        (main world map + caravan focus)
      - CaravanFormationState.cs       (Dialog_FormCaravan)
      - SplitCaravanState.cs           (Dialog_SplitCaravan)
      - CaravanInspectState.cs         (windowless caravan inspect tree)
      - CaravanInputHelper.cs          (Alt+H/M/N/G/K caravan tab dispatch)
      - CaravanUIHelper.cs             (transferable check/uncheck)
      - CaravanQuantityHelper.cs       (per-stack quantity adjust feedback)
      - CaravanFormationPatch.cs / SplitCaravanPatch.cs / CaravanAnnouncementHelper.cs
      - GearEquipMenuState.cs          (equip-this-item picker)
      - QuestLocationsBrowserState.cs / SettlementBrowserState.cs
      - StatBreakdownState.cs          (Alt+I breakdown overlay)
      - RoutePlannerState.cs           (caravan waypoint planner)
      - WorldNavigationPatch.cs / WorldObjectSelectionState.cs
      - WorldScannerState.cs           (PgUp/PgDn world map scanner)

    Shared phrases delegated elsewhere:
      - Position / Edge / Search / Stepper / Map.JumpedTo -> Common.xml
      - "Cancelled"                                       -> UI.Cancelled
      - World/scanner direction nouns                     -> Map.Direction.*
      - Pawn quick-info hotkeys ("No pawn selected")      -> Common.Guard
      - vanilla labels: caravan/settlement names, faction relations,
        biome names, pawn labels, item labels, days/hours, layer
        labels (LabelCap from LayerDef) - all from game.

    Data such as caravan names, settlement labels, pawn names, item
    labels, faction names, biome descriptions, ETA strings ("X days"),
    speed-source nouns from the game, and stat values come from the
    game's translation system and are NOT duplicated here.
  -->

